{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1786504432,"nonce":"4vSlh06DZQ0nkRwNpvVGM7qx5CY=","target":"1486286bffe519d352d5db40ea87c36f0e6efabd3acc53bd8ab281ec5d5489fb","message":"**What is wrong.** `listSources` accepts no pagination arguments at all: `export function listSources(c: Ctx = {}): Promise\u003cListEnvelope\u003cSource\u003e\u003e` at `web/src/api/endpoints.ts:451`, and `Ctx` carries exactly one field, `signal` (`endpoints.ts:78-80`). No caller can ask for a second page or a larger one, because the wrapper has nowhere to put the request.\n\nThe server is not the limitation. `listSources` in `api/openapi/openapi.yaml:2196` declares `LimitParam`, `CursorParam` and `SinceSeqParam` (`:2199-2202`) — the client simply declines all three. And `docs/design/SPEC.md:1795` (§E.1) fixes what happens then: *\"Pagination is keyset only. … `limit` default 50, max 200.\"* So `SourceReachBanner` sees the first 50 sources of the org and nothing else.\n\n**The demonstration.** `SourceReachBanner` (`web/src/components/ui/ShellBanner.tsx:116-121`) is a single `useQuery` over `listSources`, and its whole decision is a filter over that one array: `(sources.data?.data ?? []).filter((s) =\u003e s.health?.status === \"unreachable\")` at `ShellBanner.tsx:126-128`, with the strip gated on `unreachable().length \u003e 0` at `:135`. If the only unreachable source is number 51 in the sort, `unreachable()` is empty and the strip does not render.\n\nThe strip cannot even tell that it is looking at a partial list. The envelope carries `page.has_more` — `SnoozeBanner` reads exactly that field two hundred lines down (`ShellBanner.tsx:243`) and uses it to render `50+` rather than `50` — and `SourceReachBanner` never consults it. So on a truncated page it renders the healthy path, which is indistinguishable from \"oto can see everything\".\n\nThat matters because the strip is the sole surface for the §B.4 reaper guard (`docs/design/SPEC.md:207`, *\"Reaper guard (highest-value correctness rule in the system)\"*). Its own comment states the stake, `ShellBanner.tsx:94-101`: the guard *\"holds every occurrence belonging to a source oto cannot reach rather than expiring it. That is the single highest-value correctness rule in the system and it is completely invisible: the list below simply stops changing.\"* When the strip is silent for the wrong reason, an operator reads a held, frozen alert list as calm.\n\n**Why there is no minimal fix.** Two obstacles, both real.\n\n*The operation has no health filter.* `openapi.yaml:2199-2202` offers `limit`, `cursor` and `since_seq` and nothing else — there is no `health=` parameter. So completeness cannot be bought with one bigger request; it requires walking the cursor to the end of the collection on a 60-second interval (`SAFETY_NET_MS`, `ShellBanner.tsx:88`) just to answer a boolean. Raising `limit` to the §E.1 maximum of 200 would move the cliff rather than remove it, and would still be silently wrong at 201.\n\n*All three callers share one cache key.* `qk.settings.sources()` is `[\"settings\", \"sources\"]` (`web/src/api/keys.ts:72`), and it is the key for every `listSources` query in the app: `ShellBanner.tsx:118`, `web/src/features/settings/SourcesSection.tsx:174-177`, and `web/src/features/settings/TuningSection.tsx:262-265`. The live stream invalidates that same key on `source.health` (`web/src/api/live.tsx:77-78`). Giving one caller a different `limit` under the unchanged key makes the cached entry mean different things depending on which component mounted first — the settings table would render a page sized for the banner, or the banner would decide from a page sized for the table. §E.1 compounds it: a cursor embeds a filter hash `h` and is rejected `400 cursor_filter_mismatch` when the filter set differs, so a differently-parameterised read is genuinely a different collection and must not answer to the same key.\n\n**The mitigating fact.** A source is an entire registered Alertmanager (`openapi.yaml:2197`, *\"List configured Alertmanager sources\"*), not an alert or a cluster. More than fifty per org is implausible. This is a correctness gap in the strip's reasoning, not an observed live bug, and it should be prioritised as such — the value is in closing a silent failure on the system's highest-value invariant, not in fixing something operators are hitting.\n\n**Recommendation.** Two options:\n\n1. Add `health=` (enum matching `SourceHealth.status`) to the `listSources` operation, and give `SourceReachBanner` its own query — `qk.settings.sourcesByHealth(\"unreachable\")` or similar — so the strip asks the server the question it actually has.\n2. Add a dedicated count or health-summary read that returns per-status totals.\n\n**I prefer (1).** The strip does not want a count; it names up to three sources (`NAMED_SOURCES_MAX`, `ShellBanner.tsx:91`), renders each name, and hangs the upstream `last_error` off a `title` (`ShellBanner.tsx:143-151`). A summary endpoint cannot supply names or errors, so (2) either leaves the strip fetching sources anyway or needs a second round trip. A filter also fixes the cache collision as a side effect — a filtered read gets its own key by construction, which the shared-key problem above says it must have — and it stays inside the existing keyset-pagination contract instead of adding a `total`, which §E.1 forbids on unbounded collections (`SPEC.md:1795`).\n\n**Where.** `web/src/api/endpoints.ts:451` and `:78-80`, `web/src/components/ui/ShellBanner.tsx:116-135`, `api/openapi/openapi.yaml:2196-2202`, `docs/design/SPEC.md:1795` (§E.1) and `:207` (§B.4), `web/src/api/keys.ts:72`, `web/src/features/settings/SourcesSection.tsx:174-177`, `web/src/features/settings/TuningSection.tsx:262-265`.\n\n**Scope.** medium\n\n**Done when.** `SourceReachBanner`'s decision does not depend on how many sources the org has: an unreachable source that sorts past the first page still raises the strip. It reads under a cache key distinct from the two settings screens, and `SourcesSection` and `TuningSection` keep answering from `qk.settings.sources()` unchanged. If the contract gains `health=`, the generated types and validators are regenerated and `npm run generate:check` / `gen:validators:check` pass. A test in `ShellBanner.test.tsx` stubs an org whose only unreachable source is not on the first page and asserts the strip renders.","files":null}]}